# 26. One-Minute PCA Revision

Agar interview se just pehle revise karna ho:

> **PCA is an unsupervised dimensionality reduction technique. It converts many correlated/original features into fewer new features called principal components.**

> **Covariance tells how features change together.**

> **Eigenvector gives the direction.**

> **Eigenvalue tells the amount of variance in that direction.**

> **PC1 captures maximum variance, PC2 captures the next maximum variance, and so on.**

> **We usually scale the data before PCA.**

> **Number of components is commonly selected using cumulative explained variance, such as 90%, 95%, or 99%.**

> **PCA reduces dimensions but can reduce interpretability because new components are combinations of original features.**

> **For ML, fit the scaler and PCA only on training data to avoid data leakage.**

